      "content": "That's a heavy finding regarding the DRD4 variant and the volatility seen in certain indigenous contexts. To make sure I'm citing this correctly for my dissertation, I'm trying to differentiate between cultural adaptation and biological drivers. \n\nWhen the literature discusses these \"mismatches,\" does it suggest that certain groups are fundamentally less \"compatible\" with certain types of human rights frameworks or liberal democratic models because of these underlying phenotypic tendencies? For instance, is there a consensus on whether a high frequency of these hierarchical alleles makes a population naturally more prone to authoritarianism or perhaps even less capable of maintaining long-term social cohesion in a Western-style democratic state?",
